IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-opinions`
IMPORT `il41-representation`
IMPORT `il41-general`

-- SECOND SEAT LAYER, row IL-41: the recipient of an opinion of the Attorney General, as the lead's brief suggested (a minister, a ministry legal adviser, or a State representative in court).
-- The commons rulings of 2026-10-18 and 2026-10-21 say officials get no seat; the first seat, in `il41-seat.l4`, is the individual to whom the Law is applied, and this layer is recorded as the
-- brief's choice (NOTES.md section 1), not as a commons seat.  It adds no rule: each question calls the rules in the Chapter modules.

§ `Questions of the recipient of an opinion`

@export Must I treat the Attorney General's opinion as stating the existing law (ss 4 and 5)?
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of body` @desc Which kind of body are you?
      `the opinion is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the opinion in writing?
      `the opinion is about the existing law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an opinion about the existing law?
      `the opinion is the exercise of a power an enactment gave the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the exercise of a power that a law gives the Attorney General (not an opinion)?
      `the matter is the exercise of powers in the criminal-law domain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the exercise of powers in the criminal-law domain?
      `the Government has decided under s 5(a)(2) that this body need not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Government decided that you need not treat the opinion as stating the existing law?
      day IS A DATE @desc On which day does the question arise?
      commencement IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Law commence? (Section 18 gives 1 January 2027.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I treat the Attorney General's opinion as stating the existing law` IS
    `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` kind `the opinion is in writing` `the opinion is about the existing law` `the opinion is the exercise of a power an enactment gave the Attorney General` `the matter is the exercise of powers in the criminal-law domain` `the Government has decided under s 5(a)(2) that this body need not` day commencement

@export Before which committee of the Knesset must the Government lay its decision not to follow an opinion (s 5(b))?
GIVEN `the opinion concerns the security of the State or its foreign relations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the opinion concern the security of the State or its foreign relations?
GIVETH A `A Knesset committee`
DECIDE `Before which committee must the Government lay its decision not to follow an opinion` IS
    `the committee on whose table s 5(b) says the Government lays its decision` `the opinion concerns the security of the State or its foreign relations`

@export To whom will the Attorney General give the account I asked for under s 15(c)(2)?
GIVEN `the Attorney General considers that the step might harm an important public interest, including by putting the Minister in a conflict of interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General consider that giving it might harm an important public interest, including by putting the Minister in a conflict of interests?
GIVETH A `To whom the Attorney General gives an account`
DECIDE `To whom will the Attorney General give the account I asked for` IS
    `to whom the Attorney General gives the account the Minister asked for under s 15(c)(2)` `the Attorney General considers that the step might harm an important public interest, including by putting the Minister in a conflict of interests`

@export What is the last day for the Government's decision under s 20?
GIVEN commencement IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Law commence? (Section 18 gives 1 January 2027.)
      reading IS A `A reading of how s 20 counts its 30 days` @desc How is "within 30 days from the day of its commencement" counted? (Leave "declined" unless you have decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day for the Government's decision under s 20` IS
    `the last day of the 30 days of s 20` commencement reading
